WASHINGTON – The Senate Judiciary Committee today advanced the following nominations:

Joshua D. Dunlap, to be United States Circuit Judge for the First Circuit, by a vote of 12-10;

Eric Chueyee Tung, to be United States Circuit Judge for the Ninth Circuit, by a vote of 12-10;

William W. Mercer, to be United States District Judge for the District of Montana, by a vote of 12-10;

Stephen Chad Meredith, to be United States District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky, by a vote of 12-10;

Arch Capito, to be United States Attorney for the Southern District of West Virginia, by a vote of 13-9;

David Dunavant, to be United States Attorney for the Western District of Tennessee, by a vote of 15-7;

Matthew Harvey, to be United States Attorney for the Northern District of West Virginia, by a vote of 17-5;

John Heekin, to be United States Attorney for the Northern District of Florida, by a vote of 12-10;

Leif Olson, to be United States Attorney for the Northern District of Iowa, by a vote of 12-10;

Adam Sleeper, to be United States Attorney for the District of the Virgin Islands, by a vote of 17-5;

David Toepfer, to be United States Attorney for the Northern District of Ohio, by a vote of 17-5;

Ronald A. Parsons, Jr., to be United States Attorney for South Dakota, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

David Metcalf, to be United States Attorney for the Eastern District of Pennsylvania, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

Bart McKay Davis, to be United States Attorney for Idaho, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

Kurt Alme, to be United States Attorney for Montana, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

Nicolas Chase, to be United States Attorney for North Dakota, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

Lesley Murphy, to be United States Attorney for Nebraska, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

Kurt Wall, to be United States Attorney for the Middle District of Louisiana, by an en bloc vote of 16-6;

David Waterman, to be United States Attorney for the Southern District of Iowa, by a vote of 20-2;

Daniel Rosen, to be United States Attorney for Minnesota, by a vote of 20-2;

Erik Seibert, to be United States Attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia, by a vote of 20-2.

Watch the executive business meeting HERE. A recording of the judicial nominations hearing can be found HERE.

Read Chairman Chuck Grassley’s (R-Iowa) opening statement at the executive business meeting HERE, and his statement at the judicial nominations hearing HERE.

